00:06:35.240 --> 00:06:40.340
Imagine you bought a consumer stock last week after seeing a headline earnings beat estimates.

00:06:41.020 --> 00:06:47.220
Your order filled at the open but the stock dropped 4% by lunch. The mechanism behind that gap

00:06:47.220 --> 00:06:54.220
is the difference between headline EPS and the full picture in the 10Q. Revenue growth tells you

00:06:54.220 --> 00:07:01.480
if the top line is expanding while EPS can be inflated by one-time tax items or share buybacks that

00:07:01.480 --> 00:07:08.320
will not repeat. Forward guidance from management is the real signal because analysts update models

00:07:08.320 --> 00:07:14.080
within hours of the call. Check the balance sheet for rising long-term debt or falling cash.

00:07:15.040 --> 00:07:21.240
Free cash flow that diverges sharply from reported earnings is a red flag. Professionals always

00:07:21.240 --> 00:07:27.820
read the management commentary section for phrases like, we expect headwinds to persist before deciding

00:07:27.820 --> 00:07:34.340
whether the beat is sustainable. The biggest mistake with earnings is reacting only to the EPS headline.

00:07:35.000 --> 00:07:41.020
Instead, always compare actual revenue and guidance against the prior quarter and consensus estimates

00:07:41.020 --> 00:07:47.380
before adjusting position size. Before we wrap, open your brokerage screener tomorrow and filter

